      "data": {
        "label": "EXAMPLE — Security Matrix rollup demo (top / Business domain layer). Part of the Meridian Rail gallery.\n\nSwitch to the Security Matrix persona (toolbar, top-left). Four domains, one matrix, three threats:\n  • Customer Management, Payments  — 🔗 DERIVED columns. Rolled up from linked Services diagrams, which roll up from Technical-component leaves. Greyed and read-only; click a cell for the breakdown popup and an 'Open linked diagram' link.\n  • Analytics & Reporting          — ⚠ BROKEN link (points at a file that doesn't exist). Its column is hatched red and inert. Fix or remove the link on the shape.\n  • Corporate Website             — assessed DIRECTLY here (no sub-diagram). A normal editable column.\n\nUse '↻ Refresh links' after editing any leaf. Change 'Cell score' (Multiply / Add / Average) and 'Threat/vulnerability score' (Average / Sum / Max) — the active matrix's modes flow all the way down the tree, so every derived number recomputes. The completeness banner splits out how many gaps are downstream ('in linked diagrams').\n\nDetails: docs/decisions/0088-recursive-security-matrix-rollup.md"
      }
    },
